    {
      "note": "νομοθετέομαι rendered by the discontinuous hath … received the law (rule 15). Rule 91's operational test decides the head and the lemma returns no corpus unit, so rule 104 sends the query to the root family: the corpus spends *law* on νομ- in every unit, six of them in this chapter, and spends *received* on λαμβάνω, which stands untouched at 7:5, 7:8 and 7:9. So *law* glosses one element of the compound and *received* glosses nothing, which makes it the supplied light verb of a support rendering; rule 17's meaning-bearing complement and its refusal to choose a word merely because it is finite put the head there, as this chapter's other light-verb renderings do at 7:3, 7:5, 7:6, 7:9, 7:13, 7:19 and 7:25. Heading on *received* remains defensible and was the earlier reading.",
