  "review_notes": [
    "Corrected at reconciliation: νενομοθέτηται headed on received, against the chapter's eight other light-verb renderings, which all head on the complement. LEMMA=νομοθετέομαι returns no corpus unit, so rule 104's neighbouring-class query decides it: νομ- is glossed law throughout and received is what the corpus spends on λαμβάνω, present and separately aligned at 7:5, 7:8 and 7:9. The head is now law; the note names received as the competing reading.",
    "The supplied complementizer that goes to the infinitive ἀνίστασθαι under rule 85, not to any matrix verb."
  ]
